<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saint Sophia Cathedral, Polotsk</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saint Sophia Cathedral in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polotsk">Polotsk</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belarus">Belarus</a>, was built in the mid-11th century, probably under Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vseslav-of-polotsk">Vseslav of Polotsk</a>, as the principality's chief church, matching the Sophia cathedrals of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kyiv</a> and Novgorod. Damaged and rebuilt several times, it was reconstructed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baroque">Baroque</a> style for the Uniate church in the mid-18th century. It is now a museum and concert hall.</p></div>
